      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eE2Uq",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3903430502,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Customer/Application/Commands/Enrolment/BasicCustomerCommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 110,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3903430502",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "PreferredFlag is compared case-sensitively (== \"Y\"), while the rest of this flow uses the case-insensitive string extensions (e.g., Valid.Is(\"N\")). If PreferredFlag can arrive as \"y\"/whitespace, this will incorrectly suppress the email trigger. Use the existing .Is(\"Y\") helper for consistency and robustness.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated the preferred-email lookup to use PreferredFlag.Is(\"Y\"), matching the shared OrdinalIgnoreCase comparison already used elsewhere in the enrolment flow. The helper does not trim whitespace, so this resolution addresses casing consistency only."
    }
  ],
